From 7cb94a68fabb287b7279e9ca30964e5185934439 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lesommer <julien.lesommer@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:36:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] run_dino: SPMD multi-GPU (--n-devices), restart
 (--restart-from), ensemble IC (--seed), per-step timing JSONL
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Port the AISSAI JAX hackathon (Jean-Zay) additions into the standalone
production script, on the current sharded-ocean-step API:

- --n-devices N: lat-band SPMD via make_sharded_ocean_step + shard_state_latlon
  (lat-lon only; n_lat % N == 0 enforced at build; global build on host CPU
  when N > 1, the #1370 convention; forcing sharded with shard_forcing_latlon;
  rigid_lid / wind_through_step combinations refused loudly). Snapshots and
  diagnostics gather the GLOBAL state (gather_state_latlon, to_host) — the
  sharded v_lower carrier is never written to disk.
- --multicontroller / --coordinator: route-B jax.distributed via the shared
  init_multicontroller_distributed helper (before any other JAX use); requires
  --n-devices == the global device count; rank 0 is the sole writer.
- --restart-from snapshot.npz: loads a previous run's snapshot as IC
  (clock restarts at 0). Verified BIT-EXACT on a 2+2-step vs 4-step CPU smoke:
  eta/T/S/u/v max diff 0.0e+00; the planted-violation control fires.
- --seed: masked Gaussian IC perturbation for ensembles (seed=0 = canonical
  rest-state IC, byte-identical; verified 0.0 diff; seed=7 diverges as
  expected). Velocity noise projected through the face masks (the SPMD bench
  IC convention).
- --timing-jsonl: per-step wall times (compile / 5-warmup / steady mean+std),
  SYPD, Mcells/s, full provenance fields; rank 0 appends under
  multicontroller.

Smoke-verified on CPU (2 virtual devices, n_lon=16): SPMD parity vs the
single-device run within the re-association floor (eta 1.6e-5, T 1.9e-6,
u 2.1e-6 at 2 steps — under the 2e-4/1e-3 gate); all new guards fire (SPMD on
MPAS, restart on MPAS, n_lat % N != 0, multicontroller device-count mismatch).
Existing test_run_dino_config.py: 57 passed.
